5. Algorithm in Pseudocode: Find the Largest of 3 Numbers
Problem: You have 3 numbers. Find which one is largest.
Pseudocode:
BEGIN
    INPUT a, b, c
    SET largest = a
    IF b > largest THEN
        SET largest = b
    END IF
    IF c > largest THEN
        SET largest = c
    END IF
    PRINT “The largest number is”, largest
END
How it works:
Assume `a` is largest first. Check `b` and `c` one by one. If you find a bigger number, update `largest`. At the end, print the result.
